"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D2_IRAN_ORTA_ASYA:-0538-01-01:0":{"b": ["Elam (Old Elam - Neo-Elam): the Neo-Elamite period ends", "64fe1dfe"], "d": ["The Awan dynasty (c. 2400-2100 BCE), Shimashki, Epartid/sukkalmah (contemporary with Old Babylon); Middle Elam (Untash-Napirisha c. 1340-1300, Chogha Zanbil); Neo-Elam (1100-539). The name Elam first appears in a source in the text of Enmebaragesi, king of Kish (c. 2650 BCE); Neo-Elam II c. 770-646 (conflict with Assyria).", "e35bcb7b"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D2_IRAN_ORTA_ASYA:-0558-01-01:0":{"b": ["Achaemenid Empire / Cyrus II's kingdom of Persis: Cyrus II accedes to the Persian throne (559)", "c0d9c31b"], "d": ["559: beginning of Cyrus II's reign (the reign limit given by the Pasargadae article); 550: overthrow of the Median king Astyages and the unification of Iran (Schmitt); 330: the end of Darius III.", "5a8e254a"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D2_IRAN_ORTA_ASYA:-0699-01-01:0":{"b": ["Median State (centered on Hegmatana): Median state: the period of Deioces begins (Herodotean tradition)", "26e483d1"], "d": ["The political unity/state of the Medes: the Herodotean tradition begins it with Deioces (c. 700-647); the alternative Grantovskiy chronology, based on Assyrian sources, places the Median revolt at c. 672 and Deioces at c. 672/671. The last Median king Astyages was overthrown by Cyrus in 550 BCE (Median-Persian war 553-550).", "ce4a8a35"]},
