"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D2_IRAN_ORTA_ASYA:-3999-01-01:0":{"b": ["Susa: the city is founded (approximate, Iranica)", "63ff02c7"], "d": ["The center of Susiana; its foundation is given in Iranica as ca. 4000 BCE. Late Susa II (c. 3500-3100 BCE) shares the same material culture as Uruk; it is followed by the Proto-Elamite period, the Akkadian conquest (c. 2300 BCE), the incorporation into Ur III (Susa VB) and the Elamite kingdoms.", "39f0c741"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D2_IRAN_ORTA_ASYA:-4299-01-01:0":{"b": ["Anau IA and the Meana Horizon (Kopet Dag, Early Chalcolithic): Anau Ia phase (lowest layers)", "14def83f"], "d": ["A Chalcolithic after Jeitun in the Kopet Dag foothills; a separate 'Meana Horizon' preceding Anau IA was defined at Monjukli Depe (c. 4650-4340 BCE cal).", "5d2520ea"]},
