"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D3_ITALYA_AVRUPA:-0507-01-01:0":{"b": ["Rome: Monarchy -> Republic (first consuls) - WRITTEN TRADITION: Rome: the Monarchy ends, the Republic begins (traditional)", "912914d1"], "d": ["Polybius and Dionysius place the end of the Monarchy and the first consuls in the same year; three independent internal calculations (Polybius/Xerxes, Dionysius/120 years after the Gauls, Dionysius/244 years of monarchy) arrive at 508 BCE.", "59449f95"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D3_ITALYA_AVRUPA:-0669-01-01:0":{"b": ["Hallstatt C -> D transition (Dietfurt Bayesian model; traditional 616): Hallstatt C → D transition (14C model)", "e02fb9ba"], "d": ["In southern Germany the transition from Ha C to Ha D lies, according to the Bayesian model of the Dietfurt burial sequence, before 650 cal BC and most probably between 685 and 655; this is decades earlier than the commonly accepted date.", "dcfea6b4"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D3_ITALYA_AVRUPA:-0751-01-01:0":{"b": ["Foundation of Rome (dates of the WRITTEN TRADITION): foundation of Rome (written tradition, Dionysius)", "1d943e4c"], "d": ["The written tradition places the foundation of Rome, by Olympiad reckoning, in the 1st year of the 7th Olympiad (Cato, Dionysius) - between 7.1 and 12.4 across authors. Varro's 753 was NOT read FROM THE SOURCE in this session.", "181d376a"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D3_ITALYA_AVRUPA:-0759-01-01:0":{"b": ["Carthage - foundation tradition 814/813 vs archaeological ~760: Carthage: beginning of continuous occupation (archaeological)", "ee345ccd"], "d": ["The legendary foundation of Carthage (Elissa/Dido) is 814-813; continuous occupation in the city begins in the excavations at about 760 BCE, the earliest tombs belonging to the second half of the 8th century; the 8th-century necropolis has not yet been found.", "9c450808"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D3_ITALYA_AVRUPA:-0836-01-01:0":{"b": ["Latium Vetus: Latial II -> III transition (traditional ~770 vs 14C high chronology 850-825): Latium: Latial II → III transition (high chronology)", "d589d124"], "d": ["The transition from Latial II to III in the Early Iron Age of central Italy (Latium Vetus) is ~770 BCE in the traditional typo-chronology; the 14C of short-lived samples (Fidene seeds) pulls the transition to the third quarter of the 9th century BCE (850-825).", "0ed2a01a"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D3_ITALYA_AVRUPA:-0929-01-01:0":{"b": ["Greek Geometric period (absolute dates raised by 14C): Middle Geometric II begins (Sindos 14C: 930 against the traditional 800)", "900bbb4b"], "d": ["A stratigraphic animal-bone 14C series from Sindos in northern Greece raises the traditional absolute dates of the Geometric sub-phases (based on Sicilian colony dates) by 100-150 years; the beginning of MG II is 930 calBC rather than 800 histBC.", "d21e4714"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_D3_MISIR_AFRIKA:-0029-01-01:0":{"b": ["Beginning of Roman Egypt - Octavian takes Alexandria: Rome takes Egypt (Octavian)", "6ddd4666"], "d": ["August 30 BCE: Octavian takes Alexandria; the official 'kratesis' is calculated from 1 Thoth = 29 August 30 BCE (closed with the 18-day 'reign' of Antony's children).", "509e9fa3"]},
